{"created": "2026-09-27T05:01:42.632594+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-02T15:15:21.914985+00:00", "id": 22986645, "conceptrecid": "22967584", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22986645", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22967584", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22986645", "metadata": {"title": "Parity Figures as Moir\u00e9: What Is Exact and What Is Not", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22986645", "publication_date": "2026-09-27", "description": "<p class=\"MsoPlainText\">&lt;p&gt;A short note placing the parity construction of [A] (doi:10.5281/zenodo.22965031) inside the established theory of moir&eacute; (Amidror), and separating three statements usually run together. (1) The parity figure of a union of band systems is exactly the multiplicative moir&eacute; of square gratings of transmittance &plusmn;1: exclusive-or on {0,1} is multiplication on {&plusmn;1}. (2) Two printed transparencies laid on one another do not produce it: they produce the conjunction of two {0,1} gratings, which differs from the parity on 108 cells of 144 for every pair of first-generation families. (3) Two gratings of linear-polariser strips at 0&deg;/90&deg; do produce it, complemented, exactly (Malus's law: XNOR = 1 &minus; XOR). (4) The doubling homothety of [A] is the second harmonic of the cosine carrier whose level sets are the axes, not of the square-wave figures, which have odd harmonics only. Every claim is checked by a script on the published axis catalogue. Nothing new is proved; no grating was printed and no polariser cut. The measurement suggested &mdash; two polariser gratings cut from the first-generation families, viewed against a light box &mdash; would show the fifteen images of the loom of [O] (doi:10.5281/zenodo.22986529), minus their tints, one pair at a time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Licences.&lt;/strong&gt; Text and figures: CC BY 4.0. Code: AGPL v3; commercial licence on request.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Version 1.0.1.&lt;/strong&gt; References [A] and [O] corrected (deposit title and concept DOIs); licence line aligned with the record. No claim changed.&lt;/p&gt;</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Amiot, Anibal Edelberto", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0009-0002-6414-9448"}], "keywords": ["moir\u00e9", "multiplicative moir\u00e9", "parity figures", "square gratings", "polarisation moir\u00e9", "Jacquard weaving", "harmonics", "Amidror"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22965031", "relation": "isReferencedBy", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22966838", "relation": "isReferencedBy", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22945021", "relation": "isDocumentedBy", "resource_type": "publication-report", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22722485", "relation": "isReferencedBy", "resource_type": "publication-book", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/anibaledel/livreedhermes", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "1.0.1", "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/anibaledel/livreedhermes"}, "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "alternate_identifiers": [{"identifier": "Q141191562"}], "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22967584"}}]}, "notes": "<p><span><span>Code sous licence AGPL v3. Licence commerciale&nbsp;: anibaledel@gmail.com</span></span></p>"}, "title": "Parity Figures as Moir\u00e9: What Is Exact and What Is Not", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22986645", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22986645", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22986645?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22986645", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22986645", "self_doi_html": "https://z